cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use EconFlow in academic or research work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "EconFlow: Reusable panel econometrics research platform"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-19"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/abrhamgs3/econflow"
repository-code: "https://github.com/abrhamgs3/econflow"
abstract: >
  EconFlow is an open-source Python framework for reproducible cross-country
  panel econometric analyses. It provides an end-to-end pipeline covering data
  ingestion, processing, fixed-effects and IV estimation, diagnostic testing,
  and publication-ready output rendering. Originally extracted from the
  AI Adoption and Total Factor Productivity paper, it is designed to be reused
  for any longitudinal panel study.
